with the hips quiet before the shoulders unwind.","metric":{"value":"39\u00b0","caption":"shoulders past hips at the top"},"start_time":0.72,"end_time":1.05,"severity":88,"series":"separation","accent":"#F2A541","goal":{"label":"keep stretch","value":35},"focus":{"anchor":"neck","bones":["torso","neck"],"label":"Shoulders past hips","view_yaw":0}},{"id":"lead-arm","title":"Lead arm bends","headline":"Your front arm collapses at the top","plain":"At the top of the backswing your front arm bends about 44\u00b0 (it was nearly straight at address). That shortens the swing arc, so the club has less room to build speed.","why":"A bent lead arm narrows the swing radius, so the clubhead has less time to build speed.","cue":"At the top, keep the front arm long \u2014 stretch it away from your head, not chicken-winged in.","drill":"Pump drill. Pause at the top with the lead arm extended, pump down halfway twice, then swing through. Eight reps.","check":"Lead elbow flex at the top stays under 30\u00b0 instead of 44\u00b0.","metric":{"value":"44\u00b0","caption":"front-arm bend at the top"},"start_time":0.8,"end_time":1.15,"severity":72,"series":"lead-elbow","accent":"#E8C98A","goal":{"label":"address flex","value":1.1},"focus":{"anchor":"ulna_l","bones":["humerus_l","ulna_l","radius_l"],"label":"Lead arm","view_yaw":36}},{"id":"lead-arm-finish","title":"Lead arm stays bent","headline":"The front arm never fully recovers after impact","plain":"Through the finish the front arm is still bent around 65\u201370\u00b0. The arc that collapsed at the top never opens back up.","why":"If the lead arm stays collapsed after impact, you lose width through the ball and the club exits high and left of the target line.","cue":"After impact, feel the front arm extend toward the target \u2014 long and high into the finish.","drill":"Finish-hold. Hit half-swings and freeze for two counts with both arms long past the ball. Ten reps.","check":"Front-arm bend after impact drops below 40\u00b0 inste